# Two arms of arity one, both matching this package's own err, and only one of
# them is advised.
#
# `rescue` is pub, so provenance seeds it: a published err parameter is assumed
# to see its own package's failures, because the callers are not all in view.
# `quiet` is private and nobody calls it, so nothing ever feeds its parameter
# and it stays silent.
#
# The two differ only in their NAME. Provenance keys its fixpoint on
# (name, arity), and if that key ever stops distinguishing them — a collapsed
# group, a hash that ignores the name — `quiet` inherits what `rescue` was fed
# and picks up an advisory it has not earned.
type woe
  at

pub fn boom _
  err (woe 5)

pub fn rescue (err w:woe)
  w.at

fn quiet (err w:woe)
  w.at
